fimc-is2: keep sensor MCLK on and power the right module before FW boot

fimc_is_ischain_power() re-runs the module ON scenario after
fimc_is_sec_run_fw_sel(), because run_fw_sel() powers the sensor rails down
again after the EEPROM read and the firmware opens the sensor itself.

Two corrections against the earlier "pin1 handover" patch:

- Do not select pinctrl state "pin1": it maps the MCLK pin to input
  (fimc_is_mclk0_in/fimc_is_mclk1_in).  The I2C function is identical in
  pin0/pin1, so pin1 only kills MCLK.  The ON scenario already selects
  "pin0", which is the MCLK output function.
- Resolve the module from device->sensor (set by fimc_is_ischain_init_wrap
  for the module actually being initialised), not from
  core->current_position.  For the front sensor the two can differ.

Hardware evidence (J700M, stock DTB/firmware):
  j7 clk sclk_isp_sensor1 rate=26000000
  j7 mclk pad gpe1-3 func=2
  j7 mclk dat gpe1-3 ones=8802/20000   (pad toggling)
  gpe1 con=0x00002001, CMU EN_SCLK_TOP_ISP bit4=1

--- a/drivers/media/platform/exynos/fimc-is2/fimc-is-device-ischain.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/exynos/fimc-is2/fimc-is-device-ischain.c
@@ fimc_is_ischain_power(), after fimc_is_sec_run_fw_sel()
+		{
+			/* run_fw_sel() powers the sensor rails down again; the firmware
+			 * opens the sensor itself and needs them on.  Re-run the ON
+			 * scenario for the sensor the ischain is actually initialising
+			 * (device->sensor), and keep the MCLK pin in "pin0" (output). */
+			struct fimc_is_module_enum *module = NULL;
+			struct fimc_is_device_sensor *sens =
+				device->sensor ? device->sensor :
+				&core->sensor[core->current_position];
+			int sret = fimc_is_sensor_g_module(sens, &module);
+			if (!sret && module && module->pdata) {
+				if (module->pdata->gpio_cfg) {
+					int aret = module->pdata->gpio_cfg(module->pdev,
+						SENSOR_SCENARIO_NORMAL, GPIO_SCENARIO_ON);
+					info("sensor rails+pins on before FW boot: %d\n", aret);
+				}
+			} else {
+				info("sensor power lookup failed (%d)\n", sret);
+			}
+		}
